      <manifestationList xml:id="sourceDesc_N202D0">
         <manifestation label="" xml:id="source_d1e31">
            <titleStmt xml:id="titleStmt_N202D5">
               <title xml:id="title_160N2004A">Score, autograph, printer's copy</title>
            </titleStmt>
            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_N202DB">
               <extent xml:id="extent_N202DC">4 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_N202DF">34.5 x 29.5</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_N202E2">Written in brown ink. Paper: 20 staves. On two folios being a fragment of the autograph score of "Sechs Gesänge für eine Singstimme und Pianoforte, opus 55" (HartW Coll. 6). Later pagination in pencil. On p. 1 staves 5-17 bb. 1-22 of "Untreue" which has been marked with a cross in red crayon. Staves 18-20 cancelled. On p. 2 bb. 23-58, and on p. 3 staves 1-9 bb. 59-74. End-dated: "4/8 53". Above the first stave on p. 3 Hartmann has written: "dette udskrives <rend xml:id="idm34" rend="underline">ikke</rend>", which has been cancelled and changed to "jo!" [Yes] in pencil. This indicates that the manuscript was used by the printer for the printed edition. The deleted remark was probably meant for the copyist who made a copy for the Breitkopf &amp; Härtel edition of "Sechs Gesänge für eine Singstimme und Klavier, opus 55", where this song is not included.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
            <notesStmt xml:id="notesStmt_N202E8">
               <annot type="source_description" xml:id="annot_160N20065">
                  <p xml:id="idm37">On pp. 1-3 of this manuscript fragment.</p>
               </annot>
            </notesStmt>
